# wilhelmpa's sudo policy. Installed by setup.sh at /etc/sudoers.d/90-wilhelmpa,
# replacing the "wilhelmpa ALL=(ALL:ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL" rule that instance had
# before Owner Terminals existed.
#
# Why it changed: sudo authorizes purely by (user, host, command) -- it has no
# concept of which process asked, so it cannot tell an SSH session started by the
# orchestrator apart from a browser terminal's shell opened through
# volition-owner-terminal.service. Both run commands as the same Unix account,
# wilhelmpa. A blanket NOPASSWD: ALL therefore did not just cover
# `sudo -n <deploy script>` from SSH, the reason it was added -- it silently also
# made every `sudo` typed inside an owner-terminal browser session passwordless,
# defeating "sudo im Browser-Terminal verlangt Passwort" (Home -> Security,
# default on) before that setting could mean anything: there is no runtime signal
# sudo could check to tell the two apart, and NOPASSWD skips the PAM
# authentication step entirely, so nothing downstream (PAM, the owner-terminal
# service) can add the prompt back once sudoers has waived it.
#
# The clean fix is the one already used next to this file for the same reason
# (/etc/sudoers.d/91-volition-gog): stop granting NOPASSWD for ALL, and name
# exactly the automation this instance's SSH-driven workflow actually runs
# unattended. Everything else -- including these same commands run by hand, and
# any command a browser terminal session types -- falls through to the base
# `%sudo ALL=(ALL:ALL) ALL` rule in /etc/sudoers (wilhelmpa is a member of the
# `sudo` group), which asks for the Linux password every time. That password is
# `passwd`-set by the owner once; see the branch report for where.
#
# VOLITION_DEPLOY is the one command CLAUDE.md documents as run non-interactively
# over SSH today. VOLITION_STATUS is read-only (service status and logs), which
# the same workflow's "check services" step after a deploy needs and which
# carries no risk of change even without a password. Neither list is exhaustive
# of everything the orchestrator might one day want to automate -- extend it
# deliberately, one named command at a time, rather than widening back to ALL.
Cmnd_Alias VOLITION_DEPLOY = /srv/volition/source/plan-dev/deployment/volition-stack/native/deploy.sh
Cmnd_Alias VOLITION_STATUS = /usr/bin/systemctl status volition-*, /usr/bin/systemctl is-active volition-*, /usr/bin/journalctl --no-pager -u volition-*

wilhelmpa ALL=(ALL:ALL) NOPASSWD: VOLITION_DEPLOY, VOLITION_STATUS
